# What must NOT be sent to the Docker daemon as build context.
#
# Without this the context is about 1.6 GB, most of it things the image has no use for: .git alone is
# 479 MB of history, and node_modules is 138 MB of the React app's BUILD-time dependencies. The image
# needs the built output, not the toolchain that produced it.

# 479 MB of history. The image needs the files, not how they got there.
.git
.gitattributes

# 138 MB of build-time dependencies. The React app is already built: its output ships as
# AGENTIC-ARBITER/demo/app/, which is tracked, and that is what the server serves at /app/.
node_modules
AGENTIC-ARBITER/app/node_modules
AGENTIC-ARBITER/app/dist

# 🔴 THE KEY. Belt and braces: .env is already gitignored so it is not in a git clone, but a LOCAL
# `docker build` runs against the working tree, where it does exist. Excluded explicitly so the key
# cannot reach an image by that route either.
.env
.env.*
*.key

__pycache__
**/__pycache__
*.py[cod]
.venv
venv

# Build inputs that live outside the repository anyway. Named so that a local build does not follow
# the junctions at these paths and copy 1,026 MB the server proved it does not need.
AGENTIC-ARBITER/data/imagery
AGENTIC-ARBITER/data/weather
AGENTIC-ARBITER/data/national_fields
AGENTIC-ARBITER/data/live_cache

# ⚠ AGENTIC-ARBITER/data/geometry IS NOT EXCLUDED. 13 MB, and the server does not start without it:
# agent.py reads data/geometry/selected_site.json at import time. Measured by hiding the folder.

# The frozen copy of the old page. Useful on disk, not needed in a running image.
AGENTIC-ARBITER/preserved

# Local scratch and editor state
.claude
.vite
*.tmp
